:Namespace BigGmp

    ⎕PATH←'#.∆pmsUtils' 
    DECLARE_LIBRARIES_OPTS←'QUIET'
    LIBCHECK_QUIET←1


⍝H BigGmp - an annotated library for manipulating big integers in the GMP format.
⍝H   This library is heavily annotated to demonstrate the use of ⎕NA in managing
⍝H   a "foreign" (C-language) library.
⍝H
⍝H See subclass BigGmp.Class below...
⍝H
⍝H mpz -
⍝H mpz objects - internal "big integer" pointer objects:
⍝H Most integer GMP routines (mpz_...) require "mpz" objects, which are
⍝H generated by mpz_init routines. 
⍝H Mpz objects appear in APL as decimal integers (⎕DR 1287; ⎕NA type 'P'); 
⍝H Note: invalid use of mpz objects will likely cause the interpreter to die.
⍝H
⍝H bi - 
⍝H bi objects - APL big integer objects, either 
⍝H    [1] an APL integer, e.g. 25, ¯50, 1
⍝H    [2] a string of arbitrary length containing
⍝H        [a] an optional minus-sign, ¯ or -
⍝H        [b] any number of digits, mixed with any number of blanks
⍝H        [c] a optional prefix or suffix of the form:
⍝H            BASE     PREFIX  or   SUFFIX     DIGIT DEF.
⍝H            10       none         none       0-9
⍝H            16       X or 0X      X          0-F
⍝H             8       o or 0o      o          0-7    ⍝ Capital O ok, but looks like 0 zero
⍝H             2       B or 0B      B          0-1
⍝H            The prefix MUST follow any sign and may be in either upper or lower case.
⍝H     Valid:  '¯0X1234'  '¯X1234'  '¯1234o'   '¯0x123 4'
⍝H   Invalid:  '0X¯1234'  'B¯1101'  '¯X123o'   '¯0X123,4'
⍝H Preferred:  '¯12A4x'   '¯1101b'  '12347o'   '¯01234x'
⍝H
⍝H   Beware of APL integers which are represented as floats, such as
⍝H      1234550000000000000000000000000000000000000000
⍝H   which may be converted to a string or displayed by APL as a non-integer:
⍝H      1.23455E45
⍝H   Pass such objects as strings:  
⍝H      '1234550000000000000000000000000000000000000000' or ('123455',40⍴'0')

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←0 1 ⋄ ⎕FR←1287

  ⍝ DeclareExternalLibraries-- 
  ⍝   Generate XLib, which contains the formatted ⎕NA calls for the dynamic library
  ⍝ routines. Later, ⎕NA is called: (0⊃XLib) ⎕NA¨ (1⊃XLib)
  ⍝   Normally, documents all routines prepared for loading.
  ⍝ If Quiet is 1, no commentary is given.
  ⍝ Note: This routine is RUN to create the static library declaration list;
  ⍝       that should be required only when BigGmp is edited.
  ⍝ Note: This routine is run with args 'NOQUIET' after BigGmp is edited.
  ⍝       It normally need not be run otherwise.
    ∇ XLib←DeclareExternalLibraries Quiet;note;randStruct;reportLib;title;∆NA
      Quiet←Quiet≡'QUIET'↑⍨≢Quiet
     
      XLib←⍬ ⍬
     
      title←{Quiet:ø←0 ⋄ ⍺←1 ⋄ ⎕←' ' ⋄ stars←⍺⍴'*' ⋄ ⎕←stars,' ',⍵,' ',stars ⋄ ⎕←⎕PW⍴'—'}
      note←{Quiet:ø←0 ⋄ ⎕←' ∘ ',⍵}
     ⍝ ∆NA:  Augment Lib database for later use in ⎕NA.
     ⍝       ⍺ is used as is for left arg of ⎕NA
     ⍝       ⍵ here has (a) comments (to be removed before ⎕NA) and
     ⍝                  (b) special symbols: ∑, a size_t type, resolving to P
     ⍝       ∆NA also prints three fields: ⍺, ⍵ without comments, comments
     ⍝   For printing, consider ⍵ to have 3 fields:
     ⍝                RETURNVAL lib|EXTERNALNAME ARGDECLARATIONS ⍝ Comments
     ⍝                1             2                            3
     ⍝       LA LW1 LW2 and LC are the lengths of each of these fields...
      ∆NA←{LA LW1 LW2 LC←22 ¯20 25 35-1 ¯1 1 0     ⍝ We add 1 blank between fields
           ⍝ Split ⍵ of form   RETURNVAL lib|EXTERNALNAME ARGDECLARATIONS ⍝ Comments
           ⍝ into 3 fields:    1             2                            3
           ⍝ The first two are together the declaration w, returned as the 0th field
          declare←{
              c←(p←⍵⍳'⍝')↓⍵               ⍝ c: comments
              w←p↑⍵ ⋄ w←(-+/∧\' '=⌽w)↓w   ⍝ w: declaration w/o comments
              w1←(p←1+w⍳'|')↑w ⋄ w2←p↓w   ⍝ w up to and including '|'
              w w1 w2 c                   ⍝ w after '|'
          }
           ⍝ simple formatted report of declaration
          report←{tk←{(|⍺)≥≢⍵:⍺↑⍵ ⋄ (⍵↑⍨⍺-1),'! '} ⋄ pad←3⍴' '
              Quiet:ø←0 ⋄ ⊢⎕←pad,(LA tk ⍺~' '),' ',(LW1 tk 0⊃⍵),' ',(LW2 tk 1⊃⍵),' ',(LC tk 2⊃⍵)
          }
          w w1 w2 c←declare ⍵
          ø←⍺ report w1 w2 c
          ((w='∑')/w)←'P'
          (0⊃XLib),←⊂⍺
          (1⊃XLib),←⊂w
      }
     
      ⍝⍝⍝ BEGIN STATIC LIBRARY LOAD
       ⍝ THIS SECTION CONTAINS GMP LIBRARY DECLARATIONS...
       ⍝ We group them into one large set of library declarations at compile time...
      :Section GMP LIBRARY
          0 title'DECLARATION OF EXTERNAL LIBRARIES'
          1 title'GMP LIBRARY.           Note Special Type: ∑ = size_t, 8 bytes. Most P''s = mpz ptrs'
          2 title'Initialization and Cleanup Routines'
          title curLib←'libgmp.dylib'       ⍝ The GMP big number library ...
          'mpz_init'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_init P'
          'mpz_sizeinbase'∆NA'∑ ',curLib,'|__gmpz_sizeinbase P I     ⍝ ∑ = size_t'
          'mpz_set_str'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_set_str P <0C I'
          'mpz_init_set_str'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_init_set_str P <0C I'
          'mpz_set_si'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_set_si P I8'
          'mpz_init_set_si'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_init_set_si P I8'
          'mpz_realloc2'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_realloc2 P U8'
          'mpz_clear'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_clear P'
     
          2 title'ADDITION, SUBTRACTION, AND MULTIPLICATION'
          'mpz_add'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_add P P P'
          'mpz_sub'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_sub P P P'
          'mpz_sub_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_sub_ui P P U8'
          'mpz_ui_sub'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_ui_sub P U8 P'
          'mpz_mul'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_mul P P P'
          'mpz_mul_si'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_mul_si P P I8'
          'mpz_mul_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_mul_ui P P U8'
     
          2 title'ADD-MUL, SUB-MUL etc'
          'mpz_addmul'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_addmul P P P'
          'mpz_addmul_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_addmul_ui P P U8'
          'mpz_submul'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_submul P P P'
          'mpz_submul_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_submul_ui P P U8'
          'mpz_mul_2exp'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_mul_2exp P P U8'
          'mpz_neg'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_neg P P'
          'mpz_abs'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_abs P P'
     
          2 title'DIVISION LIBRARY'
          note'Groups: C/eiling, F/loor, T/runcate'
          note'Returns: q/otient, r/emainder'
          note'Do not call these directly. APL versions trap divide by 0 in APL to avoid interpreter failure'
          'mpz_size'∆NA'∑ ',curLib,'|__gmpz_size P              ⍝ ∑ = size_t'
          '_mpz_cdiv_q'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_cdiv_q P P P'
          '_mpz_cdiv_r'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_cdiv_r P P P'
          '_mpz_fdiv_q'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_fdiv_q P P P'
          '_mpz_fdiv_r'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_fdiv_r P P P'
     
          '_mpz_tdiv_q'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_tdiv_q P P P'
          '_mpz_tdiv_r'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_tdiv_r P P P'
     
          2 title'Miscellaneous Functions'
     
          'mpz_mod'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_mod P P P'
          'mpz_mod_ui'∆NA'U8 ',curLib,'|__gmpz_fdiv_r_ui P P U8'
     
          'mpz_gcd'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_gcd P P P'
          'mpz_lcm'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_lcm P P P'
          'mpz_fac_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_fac_ui P U8'
     
          2 title'NOT IMPLEMENTED:    May raise div by 0; right now, we can''t trap reliably...'
          note'mpz_powm'
          note'mpz_powm_ui'
          note'mpz_powm_sec'
     
          2 title'POWER Function'
          'mpz_pow_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_pow_ui P P U8'
          'mpz_ui_pow_ui'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_ui_pow_ui P U8 U8          ⍝   P ← num*num'
          'mpz_cmp'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_cmp P P'
          'mpz_cmp_si'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_cmp_si P I8'
          'mpz_cmp_ui'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_cmp_ui P U8'
          'mpz_cmpabs'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_cmpabs P P'
          'mpz_cmpabs_ui'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_cmpabs_ui P U8'
     
          2 title'Logical and Bit Manipulation Functions'
          'mpz_and'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_and P P P'
          'mpz_ior'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_ior P P P'
          'mpz_xor'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_xor P P P'
          'mpz_com'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_com P P P                 ⍝ One''s complement'
          'mpz_popcount'∆NA'U8 ',curLib,'|__gmpz_popcount P      ⍝ Count 1 bits. Infinity if P<0'
          'mpz_setbit'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_setbit P U8'
          'mpz_clrbit'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_clrbit P U8'
          'mpz_combit'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_combit P U8                ⍝ Complement the bits'
          'mpz_tstbit'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_tstbit P U8'
          'mpz_fits_ulong_p'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_fits_ulong_p P'
          'mpz_get_ui'∆NA'P ',curLib,'|__gmpz_get_ui P'        ⍝ 1st P=unsigned long
          'mpz_probab_prime_p'∆NA'I ',curLib,'|__gmpz_probab_prime_p P I'
          'mpz_nextprime'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_nextprime P P'
     
          2 title'Random Numbers'
          '_gmp_randinit_default'∆NA curLib,'|__gmp_randinit_default P           ⍝ use gmp_randinit'
          'mpz_urandomb'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_urandomb P P U8'
          'mpz_urandomm'∆NA curLib,'|__gmpz_urandomm P P P'
     
          2 title'Loading mpz''s from bi''s'
          'mpz_get_str'∆NA'P ',curLib,'|__gmpz_get_str P I P'              ⍝ Size unknown...
          'mpz_get_strBySize'∆NA'P ',curLib,'|__gmpz_get_str >0C[] I P'        ⍝ Size known...
      :EndSection GMP LIBRARY
     
      :Section System and Dyalog libraries 
          1 title'***** System Library / Dyalog Library'
          title curLib←'libSystem.dylib'             ⍝  OS X system library...
          'strlcpy'∆NA curLib,'|strlcpy >0C[] P I'
          'memcpy_Char'∆NA curLib,'|memcpy >C[] P ∑         ⍝ ∑= size_t'
          'strlen'∆NA'∑ ',curLib,'|strlen P                ⍝ ∑= size_t'
     
          1 title curLib←'.dylib',⍨(∨/'64'⍷⊃'.'⎕WG'APLVersion')⊃'dyalog32' 'dyalog64'
          'malloc'∆NA'P ',curLib,'|malloc ∑'         ⍝ Or 2nd P...
     
         ⍝ DO NOT MOVE THIS ROUTINE: free
         ⍝ 'free' is the last library routine.
         ⍝ It is used to verify that all the library routines have been loaded...
          'free'∆NA curLib,'|free P'
     
          0 title'END DECLARE EXTERNAL LIBRARIES'
      :EndSection System Library
  ⍝⍝⍝ END STATIC LIBRARY LOAD
    ∇

    ExternalLibraryDeclarations←DeclareExternalLibraries  DECLARE_LIBRARIES_OPTS   ⍝  'QUIET' | 'NOQUIET'

  ⍝H LibCheck: Initialize the BigGmp dynamic libraries
  ⍝H              and refreshing the APL derived functions based on them (see below)
  ⍝H (void) LibCheck how
  ⍝H      how:  (1) force (flag), defaults to 0  (2) verbose (flag), defaults to 0
  ⍝H       (1) force flag is 1 if we are to load all the external fns even if they are loaded
  ⍝H       (2) verbose flag is 1 if we should report details on libraries loaded...
  ⍝H examples: 1 1 - force load with full info
  ⍝H           1 0 - force load quietly
  ⍝H           1   - same as 1 0
  ⍝H           0 0 - only load if needed, but do so quietly
  ⍝H           0   - same as 0 0
  ⍝H Returns: 1 if it loaded (forced or not), else 0
    ∇ {loaded}←LibCheck force_verbose;_;force;lastFunLoaded;note;note;libsPreloaded;reportFun;reportLib;size_t;title;verbose;∆DF;∆NA
       ⍝ External: ExternalLibraryDeclarations
     
      force verbose←2↑force_verbose         ⍝ Defaults: 0 0
     
      lastFunLoaded←⊃⌽⊃ExternalLibraryDeclarations ⍝ 'free'
      libsPreloaded←3=⎕NC lastFunLoaded
     
      →0/⍨libsPreloaded∧~force∨verbose⊣loaded←0
     
      :If verbose
          reportFun←{⍺←2 ⋄ ⎕←(⍺⍴' '),'Created APL Fun: ',⍵}
          title←{⍺←1 ⋄ stars←⍺⍴'*' ⋄ ⎕←stars,' ',⍵,' ',stars ⋄ ⎕←⎕PW⍴⎕UCS 8212}∘∊ ⍝ 8212: em-dash
          note←{⍺←3 ⋄ ⎕←(' '⍴⍨0⌈⍺-2),' ∘ ',⍵}∘∊
      :Else
          reportFun←{}
          title←{}
          note←{}
      :EndIf
     
      0 title'Verifying and Loading External and Internal (APL) Libraries and Service Routines'
      :If libsPreloaded
          title'The last LibCheck appears to have succeeded.'
          :If force
              1 title'Forcing Libraries to Initialize.'
          :Else
              :Return
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
       ⍝ (~libsPreloaded) ∨ force...
      loaded←1
     
       ⍝ Load the dynamic library functions "declared" above in DeclareExternalLibraries
      :Trap 0
          1 title'Loading External Library Functions'
          note∊'There are'(≢0⊃ExternalLibraryDeclarations)'external functions to load'
          ⎕NA¨/ExternalLibraryDeclarations
          note'Successful load of external library functions'
      :Else
          ⎕←'Loading External Library functions: Something bad happened!'
          ⎕SIGNAL/⎕DMX.(EM EN)
      :EndTrap
     
      :Section Dynamic APL Helper Functions and Declarations
          1 title'Loading Dynamic APL Helper Functions and Declarations'
       ⍝ This section contains APL Helper Functions associated with
       ⍝ the dynamic load libraries.
       ⍝ These are reloaded whenever the dynamic libraries are.
       ⍝ This is REQUIRED in some cases:
       ⍝    WHILE ⎕NA creates objects which work like niladic or monadic functions,
       ⍝    it does so by instance, not by name (apparently).
       ⍝    So, a derived function, e.g. fac_ui, built from alibrary name, here mpz_fac_ui,
       ⍝    linked to an operator, e.g.
       ⍝         fac_ui←mpz_fac_ui callGmpPU
       ⍝    will fail, if mpz_fac_ui has gone out of scope or has been reloaded.
       ⍝    For this reason, these definitions are reestablished each time the library
       ⍝    is reloaded...
     
     
          1 title'Division (÷) library helpers (to trap division by 0, etc.)'
      ⍝H Divide - c/ceiling, f/floor, t/truncate +  q/quotient r/remainder
      ⍝H We don't expose cdiv, fdiv, etc. directly. We trap divide-by-zero in advance.
      ⍝H Avoid division by zero: it terminates the APL interpreter abruptly.
      ⍝H The routines mpz_cdiv_q, cdiv_r, mdiv_q, mdiv_r are APL routines which
      ⍝H check for division by zero and call 1÷0, which can be TRAPPED via APL.
      ⍝H
      ⍝H div3Trap: Ensure 3-arg division routines avoid division by zero
      ⍝H   mpz_routine ∇ c a b
      ⍝H   c, a, b: all mpz integers. We ensure b≠0
      ⍝H If b is 0, simulates a divide by zero in APL (if done in BMP, the interpreter fails)
          reportFun'mpz_DIVFUN←_mpz_DIVFUN div3Trap     ⍝ Traps division by 0 in 3-arg lib routines'
          div3Trap←{c a b←⍵      ⍝ Routine to trap <void mpz...> fns with args <c a b>
              isZero b:1÷0       ⍝ Trap division by zero and generate APL error
              ⍺⍺ c a b           ⍝ Call 3-arg division routine
          }
      ⍝H isZero: Returns 1 if mpz passed is zero, else 1.
      ⍝H bool ← isZero mpz_Object
      ⍝H       mpz_Object - Must be a valid mpz_object (q.v.).
          reportFun'[bool]←isZero mpz      ⍝ Synonym for 0=mpz_size mpz'
          isZero←{0=mpz_size ⍵}
     
          reportFun'mpz_cdiv_q P P P    ⍝ APL-level trap for div by zero'
          mpz_cdiv_q←_mpz_cdiv_q div3Trap
     
          reportFun'mpz_cdiv_r P P P    ⍝ APL-level trap for div by zero'
          mpz_cdiv_r←_mpz_cdiv_r div3Trap
     
          reportFun'mpz_fdiv_q P P P    ⍝ APL-level trap for div by zero'
          mpz_fdiv_q←_mpz_fdiv_q div3Trap
     
          reportFun'mpz_fdiv_r P P P    ⍝ APL-level trap for div by zero'
          mpz_fdiv_r←_mpz_fdiv_r div3Trap
     
          reportFun'mpz_tdiv_q P P P    ⍝ APL-level trap for div by zero'
          mpz_tdiv_q←_mpz_tdiv_q div3Trap
     
          reportFun'mpz_tdiv_r P P P    ⍝ APL-level trap for div by zero'
          mpz_tdiv_r←_mpz_tdiv_r div3Trap
     
          reportFun'bi ← bi tdiv_q bi '
          tdiv_q←mpz_tdiv_q callGmpPPP
     
          reportFun'bi ← bi div bi               ⍝ Returns truncated quotient'
          div←tdiv_q
          note'div: "Default" division. Alias to tdiv_q:  Returns truncated quotient'
     
          tdiv_r←mpz_tdiv_r callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi tdiv_r bi '
          gcd←mpz_gcd callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi gcd bi'
          lcm←mpz_lcm callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi lcm bi'
     
       ⍝ mpz_get_int: Static, defined below
          note'mpz_get_int mpz'
          4 note'Export to an APL integer or number (float or numeric string)'
          reportFun'1 APL_integer ← mpz_get_int mpz   ⍝ On success'
          reportFun'0 0           ← mpz_get_int mpz   ⍝ On failure'
     
       ⍝ mpz_get_num: Static, defined below
          reportFun'mpz_get_num mpz:  Returns an APL number or numeric string (if exponent too large)'
     
          1 title'Random Numbers'
          note'NOT IMPLEMENTED: gmp_randinit_default. See randGetSeed,  using _gmp_randinit_default'
          reportFun'seed←randGetSeed    ⍝ Allocated a ptr to a 24-byte random seed.'
          note'seed should be freed exactly once: #.BigGmp.free seed'
     
     
          1 title'Global BigGmp.RAND_SEED is an initialized random seed ptr using GMP defaults.'
     
          {0=⎕NC'RAND_SEED':4 note'Generated NEW RANDOM SEED',RAND_SEED∘←randGetSeed
              (×RAND_SEED)∧SESSION_ID=#.sessionID:4 note'Using OLD RANDOM SEED: 'RAND_SEED
              4 note'Generated NEW RANDOM SEED',RAND_SEED∘←randGetSeed
          }⎕NULL
     ⍝⍝ DERIVED Functions:
     
          1 title'Derived functions for arithmetic  (P=pointer to mpz; U=unsigned integer)'
     
     ⍝⍝ callGmpPU-class calls
          2 title'PU-class:  bi ← fun U8'
          fac_ui←mpz_fac_ui callGmpPU ⋄ reportFun'bi ← fac_ui U8'
          2 title'PPP-class:  mpz_add P P P  ==>  bi ← bi add bi'
          add←mpz_add callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi add bi'
          sub←mpz_sub callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi sub bi'
          mul←mpz_mul callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi mul bi'
          cdiv_q←mpz_cdiv_q callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi cdiv_q bi'
          cdiv_r←mpz_cdiv_r callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi cdiv_r bi'
          fdiv_q←mpz_fdiv_q callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← bi fdiv_q bi'
          fdiv_r←mpz_fdiv_r callGmpPPP ⋄ reportFun'bi ← fdiv_r bi '
     
     ⍝⍝⍝ END  LIBRARY LOAD
     
          1 title'Object Lifecycle'
     
          reportFun'mpz ← Import bi                ⍝ Create a single NEW mpz with value bi.'
          reportFun'mpz1 mpz2 ← Import¨ bi1 bi2    ⍝ Multiple instances'
          reportFun'mpz1 ← Import 0                ⍝ Declare and create new mpz (value 0)-FAST'
          reportFun'mpz ← mpz Set bi               ⍝ Set an existing mpz to value bi'
     
     
          reportFun'bi ← Export mpz                ⍝ Creates APL version of mpz: bi←10∘_mpz2bi mpz'
     
          reportFun'Discard mpz1 mpz2 ...          ⍝ Discard a bi created with Import'
     
          1 title'Key Numbers for Experts (O/S and H/W dependent)'
          note'PTR_SIZE (Bytes for each mpz pointer):  ',PTR_SIZE
          note'SIZE_RANDOM_SEED_STRUCTURE (bytes):     ',SIZE_RANDOM_SEED_STRUCTURE
          note'Current Random Seed Pointer (RAND_SEED):',RAND_SEED
          note'BITS_PER_LIMB:                          ',BITS_PER_LIMB
          note'Last external library function loaded:  ',⊃⌽⊃ExternalLibraryDeclarations
     
     ⍝ SESSION_ID-- should be unique # once per session.
     ⍝ Required to ensure pointers are used only if created this session.
          SESSION_ID←#.∆pmsUtils.sessionID       ⍝ Dynamic- revised once per session
     
          note'SESSION_ID:                            ',SESSION_ID
          1 title'LOADING OF LIBRARY ROUTINES AND RELATED FUNCTIONS IS COMPLETE'
     
      :EndSection Dynamic APL Helper Functions and Declarations
     
    ∇

    :Section Static APL Helper Functions and Declarations
    ifUndef←{0=⎕NC ⍵:⍺ ⋄ ⎕OR ⍵}
    BITS_PER_LIMB←64

      ⍝H mpz_get_int: EXTENSION to GMP/MPZ, allowing APL to convert any object
      ⍝H    from an unsigned long, long, unsigned int, int, bit, etc. to the proper type...
      ⍝H    obviating the need for one function for ui, one for int, etc.
      ⍝H    Does NOT use floating point types...
      ⍝H    Tries to convert an mpz to an APL integer
      ⍝H    Returns (on success)  1 APL_integer
      ⍝H            (on failure)  0 0
      ⍝H int 1|0 ← mpz_get_int mpz
      mpz_get_int←{
          0≠mpz_fits_ulong_p ⍵:1(mpz_get_ui ⍵)
          0 0
      }

      ⍝H mpz_get_num: EXTENSION to GMP/MPZ, returning an APL type if possible.
      ⍝H If the exponent is too large, returns as a string.
      mpz_get_num←{⍺←34 ⋄ ndig←⍺
          ⊃ok int←mpz_get_int ⍵:int
          int←Export ⍵
          2::(1↑int),'.',(ndig↑1↓int),'E',(⍕¯1+≢int)
          ⊢float←⍎int  ⍝ If exp too large, goes to stmt above
      }

      ⍝H APLbi2Cstr_and_base: 
      ⍝H     Converts a bi (APL num string) object to:
      ⍝H        [1] a C-format string including terminating null, and 
      ⍝H        [2] the base in which the bi and C-string are encoded (as an APL int).
      ⍝H            base: 10 (default), 16, 8, 2
      ⍝H   <CString base> ← APLbi2Cstr_and_base string
      ⍝H   The string may have APL ¯ or std -. It will be replaced with a -.
      ⍝H   If the string has a prefix (with leading 0's optional and ignoring signs) or suffix:
      ⍝H        X or x:  use base 16
      ⍝H        O or o:  use base  8   (letters O or o)
      ⍝H        B or b:  use base  2   (the string must otherwise contain only 1s and 0s)
      ⍝H        else:    use base 10
      ⍝H   If more than 1 symbol appears, this order defaults: X < O < B
      ⍝H   Valid:    0X23AF3    -o21345   o¯21345   0B10010010
      ⍝H   Invalid:  023AF3     -o21348   ox21345   0B10010012
      APLbi2Cstr_and_base←{
          base←⊃10,⍨('XxOoBb'∊⍵)/16 16 8 8 2 2
           ⍝ find←{(1∊⍵∊⍺)}
           ⍝ Was:  base←⊃16 8 2 10/⍨(⍵ find'Xx')(⍵ find'Oo')(⍵ find'Bb')1
          n←{                         ⍝ Replace APL high-minus ¯ with std minus -.
              ⍵[0]='¯':n⊣n[0]←'-'⊣n←⍵
              ⍵
          }' XxBbOo'~⍨⍕⍵              ⍝ Remove any affixes or blanks...
          (n,⎕UCS 0)base              ⍝ Make C-style null-terminated string...
      }

         ⍝H aplString ← [base|10] _mpz2bi mpz
         ⍝H   Convert from GMP integer pointer to an APL string with high-minus etc.
         ⍝H   Default base is 10, but other GMP bases are allowed.
         ⍝H mpz - mpz-format big integer
         ⍝H base- See documentation, e.g. 2 (binary), 10 (default), 16 (hex), 8 (octal)

         ⍝  _mpz2bi: SHOW TWO WAYS TO GET LARGE C-STRINGS INTO APL
         ⍝  We show two options (A, here; B, below)
         ⍝
         ⍝  A: Return the string in C format (null-terminated),
         ⍝       check its length, copy into APL with known size
      _mpz2biA←{⍺←10
          base←⍺
          ~base∊2 8 10 16:⎕SIGNAL/'Export: Bases must be ∊2 8 10 16' 11
          cStr←mpz_get_str 0 base ⍵                ⍝ str is the null-string representation of ⍵
          aplStr←_CStr2APL cStr                    ⍝ Convert pointer to char * to APL string.
          aplStr[0]='-':aplStr⊣aplStr[0]←'¯'       ⍝ Convert any high-minus...
          base=10:aplStr
          base=16:aplStr,'x'      ⍝ We mark base 16 with a lc 'x' suffix...
          base=8:aplStr,'o'
          base=2:aplStr,'b'
      }
        ⍝  B: Have GMP determine the output ("Print") size, 
        ⍝     add appropriate padding for minus and null (2+),
        ⍝     then pass the explicit size when retrieving the object directly to APL
      _mpz2biB←{⍺←10
          base←⍺
          ~base∊2 8 10 16:⎕SIGNAL/'Export: Bases must be ∊2 8 10 16' 11
          lenpadded←2+mpz_sizeinbase ⍵ base        ⍝ Determine size
          aplStr←1⊃mpz_get_strBySize lenpadded base ⍵   ⍝ Get the int. string explicitly by size
          ((aplStr='-')/aplStr)←'¯'
          base=10:aplStr
          base=16:aplStr,'x'      ⍝ We mark base 16 with a lc 'x' suffix...
          base=8:aplStr,'o'
          base=2:aplStr,'b'
      }
        ⍝ The <B> algorithm appears to be about 2% faster than the <A> algorithm
    _mpz2bi←_mpz2biB 
    Export←_mpz2bi
        ⍝ Make the two options invisible...
    ⎕EX '_mpz2biA' '_mpz2biB'

      ⍝H   _CStr2APL: Takes a std (char *) C string and returns an APL char vector
      ⍝H   CVapl ← _CStr2APL P, where P points to null-terminated C string
      ⍝H   Useful in taking values returned from functions of the form: char *func.
      ⍝H   mpz_get_str is such a function (see above).
      ⍝H   NOTE: Normally used in creating library routines, not by end users.
      _CStr2APL←{
          1287≠⎕DR ⍵:'Requires a C-string pointer (APL ⎕DR 1287)'⎕SIGNAL 11
             ⍝ Convert the C-string ⍵ to an APL string, w/o the final null...
          memcpy_Char lenSizeT ⍵(lenSizeT←strlen ⍵)
      }

      ⍝H PTR_SIZE: the size of a (void *) in C. Generally 8, but can be 4.
      ⍝H GetPtrSize: function to get from APL the current pointer size: (void *)
      ⍝H I ← GetPtrSize (niladic)
    ∇ int←GetPtrSize
      int←(1∊'64'⍷⊃'.'⎕WG'APLVersion')⊃4 8
    ∇
    PTR_SIZE←GetPtrSize

      ⍝H Discard:  "free" memory associated with a list of C memory pointers,
      ⍝H            allocated via malloc. Calls mpz_clear and free on each ptr.
      ⍝H Syntax:
      ⍝H      {list_of_pointers} ← Discard list_of_pointers
      ⍝H      list_of_pointers: decimal "integers", which encode 8-Byte (void*) pointer values...
      ⍝H Note: the list of pointers MUST be from Create or directly from malloc.
      ⍝H       Freeing other space or repeatedly freeing a valid ptr will generate disaster
    ∇ {mpzN}←Discard mpzN
      mpzN←mpzN~0            ⍝ Ignore "null" mpz's (set by error-handlers below)
      →0/⍨0=≢mpzN            ⍝ If nothing to clear or free, done
      {}mpz_clear¨mpzN       ⍝ clear the GMP values
      {}free¨mpzN            ⍝ free allocated space-- catastrophic if not defined!
    ∇

      ⍝H Import: Alias for <Set ⍵> with no left argument or <0 Set ⍵>
      ⍝H         See Set. For format details, see info for APLbi2Cstr_and_base.
      ⍝H {mpz@P} ← Create <intString|int|0>
      ⍝H On failure, ⎕SIGNAL 11 (invalid integer or not a single integer).
      ⍝H Returns the mpz created and now set.
      Import←{      ⍝ Requires external PTR_SIZE (see above)
          11::⎕SIGNAL/⎕DMX.(EM EN)
          1:ø←Set ⍵
      }

        ⍝H Set:    Set an existing mpz big integer to value specifed from an APL integer or 
        ⍝H         string-format integer. See Import...
        ⍝H {mpz@P} ← mpz@P Set value:<intString|int|0
        ⍝H Returns: mpz originally passed
      Set←{⍝ ⍺: mpz, ⍵: value
          ⍺←0 ⋄ PTR ALLOC_LVL←0
          11::⎕SIGNAL/⎕DMX.(EM EN)⊣ALLOC_LVL{
              ⍺=1:free ⍵             ⍝ Partial allocation...
              ⍺=2:free ⍵⊣mpz_clear ⍵ ⍝ Full allocation...
              ⍬                      ⍝ No allocation...
          }PTR
          mpz didAlloc←{  ⍝ Allocate ptr, prepared to free storage if error...
              0≠⍵:⍵ 0
              0=mpz←malloc PTR_SIZE:Set_eMsgLA ⎕SIGNAL 11
              ALLOC_LVL∘←1 ⋄ PTR∘←mpz ⍝ PTR can't be null if here...
              ø←mpz_init mpz ⋄ ALLOC_LVL∘←2
              mpz 1
          }⍺
          setString←{ ⍝ String format... Returns ptr if obj ⍵ valid
              str base←APLbi2Cstr_and_base ⍵
              rc←mpz_set_str ⍺ str base
              0=rc:⍺                          ⍝ rc=¯1?
              Set_eMsginit ⎕SIGNAL 11         ⍝ → Error on conversion of string
          }                                ⍝ value           treat as
          0=≢⍵:ø←mpz⊣mpz_set_si mpz 0      ⍝  ⍬|''            0
          ' '=1↑0⍴⍵:ø←mpz setString ⍵      ⍝ string           string
          1≠≢⍵:Set_eMsgScalar ⎕SIGNAL 11   ⍝ num vec          ERROR
          ⍵≠⌊⍵:Set_eMsgInt ⎕SIGNAL 11      ⍝ float            ERROR
          didAlloc∧⍵=0:ø←mpz               ⍝ 0 and didAlloc   fast: mpz_init already init'd
          1:ø←mpz⊣mpz_set_si mpz ⍵         ⍝ int              int
      }
    Set_eMsgLA←'Set requires an mpz (big integer pointer) as left argument'
    Set_eMsginit←'Invalid BigGmp string-format integer (input to mpz_set_str)'
    Set_eMsgScalar←'Only a single scalar integer is allowed.',⎕TC[2]
    Set_eMsgScalar,←'Did you do "A B Set val1 val2", but mean "A B Set¨ Val1 val2"?'
    Set_eMsgInt←'APL number not a valid integer. Use string format for large integers.'


    SIZE_RANDOM_SEED_STRUCTURE←24     ⍝ sizeof structure {P P P}
      _randGetSeed←{seed←malloc SIZE_RANDOM_SEED_STRUCTURE
          ø←_gmp_randinit_default seed  ⍝ Initialize rand # gen
          seed
               ⍝ Free via:   #.BigGmp.free seed (exactly once!)
      }
        ⍝ randGetSeed - initialize random # generator pointer
        ⍝ Free (once) via 
        ⍝     BigGmp.free ptr 
        ⍝ From APL it is just passed where required as a "black box" pointer.
        ⍝ To save its contents, save its structured contents {P P P}
    ∇ ptr←randGetSeed
      ptr←_randGetSeed ⍬
    ∇

    :EndSection Static APL Helper Functions and Declarations

⍝ THE WORK!!!
    ⍝H BigGmp.add:  Add two "big" signed integers (up to thousands of digits)
    ⍝H cIntS←aIntX add bIntX
    ⍝H    aIntX, bIntX: an APL integer or a string-format integer with ¯ or -.
    ⍝H          e.g. 453 ¯10102 '999934343' '-44444' '¯44444' (10000⍴⎕D)
    ⍝H    cIntS:        a string-format integer with ¯
    ⍝H  Beware passing large, APL integers; this one 
    ⍝H    24234224241441423423423134324414114
    ⍝H  is likely to be treated as
    ⍝H    2.42342242414414234234231343244141E34
    ⍝H  which will be treated as an (invalid) float.
    ⍝H  Better, quote it: '24234224241441423423423134324414114'

    :Section Convenience Functions
    ⍝ Here, we take the prototype FORM3 and create 3-argument calls:
    ⍝    add, sub, mul, ...

    ⍝H Trap routine for callGmpPPP, ~PP, ~PU (q.v.)
    ⍝H ∆TrapMath is a function, so found in ⎕PATH
    ∇ t←∆TrapMath funNames
         ⍝ Local to calling function: funNames in the form 'name1 name2 name3 ...'
         ⍝ e.g.   ⎕TRAP←∆TrapMath 'A B C'
      t←(1 11)'C'('(⎕DMX.(EM,'' '',Message))⎕SIGNAL ⎕DMX.EN⊣#.BigGmp.Discard ',funNames)
    ∇



    ∇ c←a(mpzFunc callGmpPPP)b;A;B;C;⎕TRAP
      A B C←0 ⍝ Set A B C to 0 for error handling before any statement that might ⎕TRAP
      ⎕TRAP←∆TrapMath'A B C'
      LibCheck 0
      C A B←Import¨0 a b           ⍝ Create and initialize result c
      {}mpzFunc C A B              ⍝ c ← a + b
      c←Export C                   ⍝ Convert pointer c to APL numeric string...
      Discard A B C                ⍝ Cleanup (free etc) what a, b, c point to
    ∇

    ∇ c←(mpzFunc callGmpPP)b;B;C;⎕TRAP
      B C←0
      ⎕TRAP←∆TrapMath'B C'
      LibCheck 0
      C B←Import¨0 b               ⍝ Create and initialize result c
      {}mpzFunc C B                ⍝ c ← a + b
      c←Export C                   ⍝ Convert pointer c to APL numeric string...
      Discard B C                  ⍝ Cleanup (free etc) what a, b, c point to
    ∇

    ∇ c←(mpzFunc callGmpPU)b;C;⎕TRAP
      C←0
      ⎕TRAP←∆TrapMath'C'
      LibCheck 0
      C←Import 0
      {}mpzFunc C b
      c←Export C
      {}Discard C
    ∇


        ⍝H SAMPLE ROUTINE...
        ⍝H sum: Sum an arbitrary list of APL Big Integer strings (bi)
        ⍝H intString ←  [maxBitGuess | 10000] BigGmp.sum bi bi ... 
        ⍝H WARNING: Preallocation should use mpz_ internal routine per best practice.
    ∇ c←{maxBitGuess}sum BList;B;C;a;nums;⎕TRAP;⎕PATH
      ⎕PATH←'#.BigGmp'
      ⎕TRAP←∆TrapMath'B C'
      maxBitGuess←10000 ifUndef'maxBitGuess'
     
      C B←Import¨0 0            ⍝
      {}mpz_realloc2 C(maxBitGuess)  ⍝ Guess on a size for C to reduce reallocation
      {}C Set 0⊃BList
      {}{mpz_add C C(B Set ⍵)}¨1↓BList
      c←Export C
      Discard B C
    ∇

    ⍝⍝----------------------------------------------------------------------------------⍝⍝
    ⍝⍝----------------------------------------------------------------------------------⍝⍝
    LibCheck 1 ,(~LIBCHECK_QUIET)   ⍝ 0 0 - NOFORCE QUIET.  1 1 - FORCE NOISY.    1 0 - FORCE QUIET  ⍝⍝
    ⍝⍝----------------------------------------------------------------------------------⍝⍝
    ⍝⍝----------------------------------------------------------------------------------⍝⍝

    :EndSection  ⍝ Convenience Functions

    :Section BigGmp.Class
    :Class Class
        ⎕PATH←'#.BigGmp #.∆pmsUtils'   ⍝ ??? 
        UTIL←#.BigGmp 

        ⎕IO ⎕ML←0 1 ⋄ ⎕FR←1287 ⋄ ⎕PP←34

        :Field Private _Ptr←0       ⍝ 0= no object created or value set
        :Field Private _BaseOut←16  ⍝ Default is base 16... (FAST)
        :Field Private _Value←⍬     ⍝ ⍬= no value known (might need to be retrieved)
        :Field Private _SessionID←0 ⍝ 0= no session active.

         ⍝  o ← ⎕NEW BigGmp.Class
         ⍝  Same as 
         ⍝    o ← ⎕NEW BigGmp.Class 0
        ∇ createFromNull            ⍝ No arg; Same as zero...
          :Implements Constructor
          :Access Public
          _Create 0
        ∇


         ⍝  o ← ⎕NEW BigGmp.Class value
         ⍝  value: ⍝ (BigGmp.Class object | string | APL signed int)
         ⍝  
        ∇ createFromValue value
          :Implements Constructor
          :Access Public
          _Create value
        ∇

            ⍝ _Create: service function for ⎕NEW Constructors
            ⍝  memAllocate←1  ∇   value
            ⍝     memAllocate: 1: Do allocate an mpz object using malloc and mpz_init
            ⍝                  0: Do not allocate such an object, 
            ⍝                     UNLESS the ptr is not current (i.e. is from a prior session)
            ⍝     value: As for create_FromValue
            ⍝  Note: does atomically:
            ⍝        ptr←malloc ... ⋄ _←mpz_init ptr
            ⍝  If either part fails, ptr guaranteed to be 0.
            ⍝  See destroy (the Class Destructor)

        ∆Create_EMSG1←'Declarations must be from integers, integer string, or BigGmp objects'
        ∆Create_EMSG2←'Unable to retrieve value of BigGmp number'
        ∆Create_EMSG3←'Tried to retrieve field ⍵.Value from non-BigGmp object'
        ∆Create_EMSG4←'Unable to allocate space for mpz value (malloc or mpz_init)'

        ∇ {memAllocate}_Create fromValue;nc;v;⎕TRAP;∆EMSG
          memAllocate←1 ifUndef'memAllocate'
         
          ⎕TRAP←0 'C' '(''BigGmp: '',⎕DMX.EM,'' '',∆EMSG) ⎕SIGNAL/ ⎕DMX.EN'
         
          ∆EMSG←∆Create_EMSG1
         
          :If 2=⌊nc←⎕NC⊂'fromValue'        ⍝ A simple value: string or number
              :If 0=≢_Value ⋄ _Value←0 ⋄ :EndIf   ⍝ '' or ⍬ → 0
          :ElseIf 9.2=nc                   ⍝ A class instance?
              :If ⎕THIS=⎕CLASS fromValue   ⍝ a BigGmp.Class object
                  ∆EMSG←∆Create_EMSG2
                  v←fromValue.Value
              :Else                        ⍝ Not BigGmp, but it may have a Value field
                  ∆EMSG←∆Create_EMSG3
                  v←fromValue.Value
              :EndIf
          :Else                            ⍝ Not a type we can handle
              ∆Create_EMSG1 ⎕SIGNAL 11
          :EndIf
         
          ∆EMSG←∆Create_EMSG1
          :If memAllocate                   ⍝ allocate=1 (default)
          :OrIf ~IsCurrentPtr                   ⍝ Obj has old ptr?
              _SessionID←UTIL.SESSION_ID      ⍝ Must set BEFORE ptr initialization
              :Trap 99  ⍝ Shld be 0...
                  'here2' ⋄ ⎕DL 1
                  _Ptr←UTIL.malloc UTIL.PTR_SIZE      ⍝ Allocate and get the mpz pointer
                  ∆Create_EMSG4 ⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨0=_Ptr
                  _←UTIL.mpz_init _Ptr              ⍝ mpz now safe with value 0
              :Else
                  ⎕SIGNAL/∆Create_EMSG4{(⍺,': ',⍵.EM)⍵.EN}⎕DMX
              :EndTrap
          :EndIf
         
          _Ptr Set _Value←v
          ⎕DF'[BigGmp ',(⍕_Value),']'
        ∇
⍝ -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ⍝
⍝   C L A S S      D E S T R U C T O R
⍝ -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ⍝
        ∇ destroy;p
          :Implements Destructor
             ⍝ Destroy will clean up:
             ⍝ If _Ptr≠0, then...
             ⍝        (a) call mpz_clear _Ptr and set __STATE←1
             ⍝        (b) free _Ptr
             ⍝ Otherwise: quietly clears _Ptr, _SessionID, _Value, and __STATE
          :If ×_Ptr
              UTIL.mpz_clear _Ptr       ⍝ clear the GMP values
              UTIL.free _Ptr
          :EndIf
          _Ptr←_SessionID←0 ⋄ _Value←⍬
        ∇

⍝ -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ⍝
⍝   C L A S S      M E T H O D S
⍝ -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ⍝
            ⍝ Value (get) - 
            ⍝   if up to date,
            ⍝         returns the current _Value, 
            ⍝   otherwise, 
            ⍝      if the pointer is up to date, 
            ⍝         retrieves it from GMP, 
            ⍝      otherwise, returns numeric 0
            ⍝ Note: Does not update _Ptr in every case. To do that, get Ptr...
        :Property Value
        :Access Public Instance 
            ∇ v←get
              :If ×≢_Value    ⍝ Has known _Value, use it...
                  v←_Value
              :ElseIf Ptr≠0   ⍝ Ptr:get will create initial value if out of date
                  v←_Value←_BaseOut UTIL.Export _Ptr
              :Else
                  _Create 0   ⍝ Sets _Ptr, _Value, _SessionID
                  v←_Value
              :EndIf
            ∇
                ⍝ set value
                ⍝    value:  a BigGmp object, a string value, an APL integer
                ⍝ If ⍵ is a BigGmp object, then these are the same:
                ⍝    my.Value ← ⍵   OR    my.Value ← ⍵.Value 
            ∇ set value
              0 _Create value
            ∇
        :EndProperty ⍝ Value

          ⍝ Ptr: Returns the current MPZ pointer, if non-zero and up-to-date,
          ⍝      otherwise creates a new MPZ with value 0 and returns its pointer
          ⍝      Always returns a valid pointer, unless it fails...
          ⍝ Note: Does not update _Value in every case. To do that, get Value...
        Ptr_EMSG1←'BigGmp: It is invalid to set the Ptr value directly'
        Ptr_EMSG2←'BigGmp: SetOutputBase bases ∊ 16 10 8 2'
        :Property Ptr
        :Access Public Instance
            ∇ p←get
              :If ~IsCurrentPtr
                  :If 0=≢_Value ⋄ _Value←0 ⋄ :EndIf
                  _Create _Value    ⍝ Sets _Ptr, _Value, _SessionID
              :EndIf
              p←_Ptr
            ∇
            ∇ set value
              Ptr_EMSG1 ⎕SIGNAL 11
            ∇
        :EndProperty ⍝ Ptr 

        ∇ SetOutputBase base
          :Access Public  
          :Trap 0
              _BaseOut←(base∊16 10 8 2)↑base
          :Else
              Ptr_EMSG2 ⎕SIGNAL 11
          :EndTrap
        ∇

        ∇ ok←IsCurrentPtr
          :Access Public 
          ok←(_Ptr≠0)∧(_SessionID=UTIL.SESSION_ID)
        ∇

    :EndClass ⍝ BigGmp.Class
    :EndSection ⍝ BigGmp.Class

:EndNamespace
